From 36d9e7bfbf144747209d9fb3341c94e306a7f9ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen35 <qwen35@local>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:09:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [GPU] Fold RMSNorm into DynamicQuantize

The weight-compressed FullyConnected path quantises its activation with DynamicQuantize
(symmetric i8, group 128). For 47 of the 48 pre-GEMM RMSNorms of Qwen3.5-2B the
RMSNorm output is consumed only by that DynamicQuantize, so the normalised f16 tensor is
written and read back for nothing.

* DynamicQuantize gets `fused_rms` / `rms_eps` attributes (hash, ==, save/load).
* prepare_primitive_fusing: new fuse_rms_into_dynamic_quantize pass (symmetric i8, group
  128, identity order, power-of-two row <= 32 x 128 elements, gamma covers the row, f16,
  affine RMS with a single consumer; also supports the precomputed-reduction (INT8
  weight-only) variant).
* dynamic_quantize_gpu_opt.cl: FUSE_RMS path = reduction, normalisation and gamma in
  registers, f16 rounding at the original boundary, then quantisation. The ref and
  kv-cache kernels refuse fused_rms.
* A folded node cannot be skipped to the f16 pass-through at batch 1, so decode quantises
  at those sites (INT8 TPOT +0.3 ms).

Unit test: fused_rms_matches_separate_rms_and_dq (bit-exact vs the separate kernels).
